ry}\\label{source-repository}\n  \n  All source files are available at:\n  \\url{https://github.com/robert2100-08-16/Mars}\n  \n  \\subsubsection{Typography Notes}\\label{typography-notes}\n  \n  The PDF uses DejaVu fonts for broad Unicode coverage across Latin,\n  Greek, Cyrillic and mathematical symbol ranges. Colour emojis are\n  rendered via the Twemoji Mozilla font using the COLR/CPAL format\n  supported by LuaLaTeX.\n  \n  Mathematical notation uses LaTeX’s native math typesetting. Chemical\n  formulae (CO\\(_2\\), SiO\\(_2\\), H\\(_2\\)O, etc.) are rendered as Unicode\n  subscripts where supported, with LaTeX math-mode fallback in the PDF.\n  \n  \\subsubsection{Paper Format}\\label{paper-format}\n  \n  A4, 2.5 cm margins, 11 pt body text, numbered sections, hyperlinked\n  cross-references and table of contents.\n  \n  \\subsubsection{Version History}\\label{version-history}\n  \n  \\begin{longtable}[]{@{}lll@{}}\n  \\toprule\\noalign{}\n  Version & Date & Notes \\\\\n  \\midrule\\noalign{}\n  \\endhead\n  \\bottomrule\\noalign{}\n  \\endlastfoot\n  1.0.0 & 2026-02-08 & First edition \\\\\n  \\end{longtable}\n  \n  \\newpage\n  \n  \\chapter{The Mars Book}\\label{the-mars-book}\n  \n  \\textbf{Collected Papers, Concepts and Engineering Studies on Mars\n  Habitats, Biomimetic Structures and Autonomous Robotics}\n  \n  \\begin{center}\\rule{0.5\\linewidth}{0.5pt}\\end{center}\n  \n  \\emph{Robert Alexander Massinger} Robert Alexander Massinger Space\n  Technologies Munich, Germany\n  \n  \\begin{center}\\rule{0.5\\linewidth}{0.5pt}\\end{center}\n  \n  Version 1.0.0 · February 2026\n  \n  \\begin{center}\\rule{0.5\\linewidth}{0.5pt}\\end{center}\n  \n  \\begin{quote}\n  \\emph{“Mars is there, waiting to be reached.”} — Buzz Aldrin\n  \\end{quote}\n  \n  \\begin{center}\\rule{0.5\\linewidth}{0.5pt}\\end{center}\n  \n  This book brings together the author’s published papers, design concepts\n  and engineering studies developed between 2024 and 2026. The work spans\n  three domains: inflatable rubber-glass habitats that can shelter early\n  settlers, biomimetic materials that may one day grow themselves, and\n  autonomous robots that prepare the terrain before humans arrive.\n  \n  Every chapter can be read independently. Where a chapter has been\n  published as a standalone paper on Zenodo, its DOI is printed in the\n  chapter header.\n  \n  \\panEmoji{📄} Licensed under \\textbf{Creative Commons Attribution 4.0\n  International (CC BY 4.0)}\n  \n  \\panEmoji{🌐} Repository:\n  \\href{https://github.com/robert2100-08-16/Mars}{github.com/robert2100-08-16/Mars}\n  \n  \\newpage\n  \n  \\chapter{Summary}\\label{summary}\n  \n  \\begin{itemize}\n  \\tightlist\n  \\item\n    \\hyperref[md-readme]{The Mars Book}\n  \n    \\begin{itemize}\n    \\tightlist\n    \\item\n      \\hyperref[md-chapters-cost-estimation-readme]{1. \\textbf{Test\n      Project on Earth}}\n    \\item\n      \\hyperref[md-chapters-design-rubber-glass-house-readme]{1. Concept\n      and Design}\n    \\item\n      \\hyperref[md-chapters-variants-rubber-glass-house-readme]{1.\n      Two-Story Rubber-Glass House}\n    \\item\n      \\hyperref[md-appendix-colophon-readme]{Colophon}\n    \\item\n      \\hyperref[md-chapters-design-improvements-v2-readme]{Design\n      Improvements for the Mars Rubber-Glass House – Proposals for v2}\n    \\item\n      \\hyperref[md-appendix-license-readme]{License}\n    \\item\n      \\hyperref[md-chapters-mars-field-laboratories-readme]{Mars Field\n      Laboratories: Integrating Autonomous Legged Robots and Cooperative\n      Robotic Clusters (Version 1.2)}\n    \\item\n      \\hyperref[md-chapters-the-peoples-house-readme]{README}\n    \\item\n      \\hyperref[md-chapters-three-step-evolution-readme]{Three-Step\n      Evolution Towards Biomimetic and Self-Growing Structures: A Vision\n      for Adaptive Habitats on Mars}\n    \\end{itemize}\n  \\item\n    \\hyperref[md-introduction-readme]{Introduction}\n  \\end{itemize}\n  \n  \\e