  \paragraph{2.3 Thermal Zoning}\label{thermal-zoning}
  
  Three climate zones separated by lightweight silicone foam partition
  walls (STC ≥ 35):
  
  \begin{verbatim}
  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                    SOLAR ROOF (1000 m²)              │
  │              + 50 cm Martian regolith layer          │
  ├──────────┬──────────────────────┬────────────────────┤
  │          │                      │                    │
  │  WARM    │    TEMPERATE         │      COOL          │
  │  ZONE    │    ZONE              │      ZONE          │
  │  ~350 m² │    ~250 m²           │      ~400 m²       │
  │  22–24°C │    18–20°C           │      12–16°C       │
  │          │                      │                    │
  │ Living   │ Labs, workshops,     │ Agriculture,       │
  │ quarters,│ machinery room,      │ vertical farming,  │
  │ kitchen, │ medical bay,         │ algae bioreactors, │
  │ cabins,  │ ISRU processing,     │ aquaponics,        │
  │ quiet rm │ waste processing     │ composting         │
  │          │                      │                    │
  │ [Airlock │                      │         [Airlock   │
  │  NORTH]  │                      │          SOUTH]    │
  ├──────────┴──────────────────────┴────────────────────┤
  │  MEZZANINE LEVEL (above warm + temperate zones)      │
  │  ~400 m²: 4 crew cabins (48 m²), quiet room (12 m²), │
  │  storage, crew recreation, vertical farm upper tiers │
  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
  \end{verbatim}
  
  \textbf{Energy savings:} Estimated 20–30\% reduction in heating load
  compared to uniform heating, as the agricultural zone (40\% of floor
  area) operates at 12–16 °C with day/night cycling.
  
  \begin{center}\rule{0.5\linewidth}{0.5pt}\end{center}
  
  \subsubsection{3. Closed-Loop Life Support System
  (CLLSS)}\label{closed-loop-life-support-system-cllss}
  
  The v2.0 habitat operates as a near-closed bioregenerative life-support
  system. The goal is \textbf{≥ 95\% closure} for water and \textbf{≥ 80\%
  closure} for food, following the Biosphere 2 model but improved with 30
  years of subsequent research.
  
  \paragraph{3.1 Atmospheric Management}\label{atmospheric-management}
  
  \begin{longtable}[]{@{}
    >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\linewidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.3333}}
    >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\linewidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.3333}}
    >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\linewidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.3333}}@{}}
  \toprule\noalign{}
  \begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
