  \paragraph{4.3 Aquaponics Integration}\label{aquaponics-integration}
  
  A closed-loop fish–plant system provides protein diversification and
  nutrient cycling:
  
  \begin{verbatim}
  ┌─────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐
  │  Fish Tanks │────>│ Biofilter    │────>│ Grow Beds    │
  │  (Tilapia)  │     │ (NH_{3}→NO_{3}⁻)   │     │ (Lettuce,    │
  │  30 m²      │     │              │     │  tomatoes)   │
  │  28°C       │     └──────────────┘     │              │
  │             │<─────────────────────────│ Return water │
  └─────────────┘                          └──────────────┘
        │                                         │
        ▼                                         ▼
    Fish waste                              Clean water
    (fertiliser)                            (back to tanks)
  \end{verbatim}
  
  \begin{itemize}
  \tightlist
  \item
    \textbf{Fish species:} Tilapia (\emph{Oreochromis niloticus}) — hardy,
    fast-growing, omnivorous, previously used in Biosphere 2’s rice–azolla
    pond system
  \item
    \textbf{Feed:} Spirulina + crop residue + insect meal (black soldier
    fly larvae fed on food waste)
  \item
    \textbf{Yield:} \textasciitilde120 kg fish/year (30 g protein/day for
    4 crew)
  \end{itemize}
  
  \paragraph{4.4 Lighting System}\label{lighting-system}
  
  Mars receives only \textasciitilde43\% of Earth’s solar irradiance (590
  W/m² peak at Mars vs.~1,361 W/m²). During global dust storms (lasting
  2–8 weeks), solar input can drop to 10–20\% of nominal.
  
  \textbf{Supplemental LED array:} - Full-spectrum LEDs (red 660 nm + blue
  450 nm + white) — optimised for photosynthetically active radiation
  (PAR) - Power requirement: \textasciitilde50 W/m² × 1,200 m² effective
  area × 18 h/day = \textbf{1,080 kWh/day} at full power - During clear
  conditions: LEDs supplement natural sunlight (reduce to
  \textasciitilde30\% power) - During dust storms: LEDs operate at 100\%
  to maintain crop growth - Light scheduling: 18 h light / 6 h dark cycle
  (optimised for most crop species)
  
