  \paragraph{9.2 Psychological Support
  Framework}\label{psychological-support-framework}
  
  Drawing on lessons from all analogues:
  
  \begin{longtable}[]{@{}
    >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\linewidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.3333}}
    >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\linewidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.3333}}
    >{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{(\linewidth - 4\tabcolsep) * \real{0.3333}}@{}}
  \toprule\noalign{}
  \begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
  Stressor
  \end{minipage} & \begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
  Mitigation
  \end{minipage} & \begin{minipage}[b]{\linewidth}\raggedright
  Evidence
  \end{minipage} \\
  \midrule\noalign{}
  \endhead
  \bottomrule\noalign{}
  \endlastfoot
  \textbf{Isolation} & Weekly Earth video calls; crew social events;
  varied daily activities & MARS-500: crew spent increasing time alone;
  ISS: scheduled family calls essential \\
  \textbf{Confinement} & 5 m ceiling height; glass walls with exterior
  views; varied thermal zones; EVA opportunities & Submarines/Antarctic:
  perceived spaciousness correlates with morale \\
  \textbf{Interpersonal conflict} & Conflict resolution training
  pre-mission; private cabins; quiet room; monthly psychology review &
  Biosphere 2: crew split into two factions; prevention is key \\
  \textbf{Monotony} & Rotating task assignments; hobby supplies; musical
  instruments; virtual reality recreation; celebration of holidays and
  milestones & HI-SEAS: 40 tasks/week maintained engagement; celebrations
  important \\
  \textbf{Circadian disruption} & Strict light scheduling (blue-light
  curfew at 20:00); dedicated sleep cabins with blackout; morning
  bright-light exposure & Concordia + MARS-500: circadian disruption is
  universal in isolation \\
  \textbf{Loss of purpose} & Clear mission objectives; science publication
  goals; shared responsibility for food production; mentoring roles & ISS:
  crew who feel scientifically productive report higher satisfaction \\
  \textbf{Health anxiety} & Regular medical monitoring; telemedicine
  access; comprehensive pharmacy; cross-training in basic medical skills
  for all crew & All analogues: medical training for non-doctors is
  essential \\
