#### 4. Agricultural System

##### 4.1 Design Parameters

| Parameter | v1 | v2.0 |
|---|---|---|
| Base agricultural area | 200 m² (50 m²/person) | **400 m² (100 m²/person)** |
| Vertical tiers | 1 | **3 tiers in cool zone** |
| Effective growing area | 200 m² | **~1,200 m²** |
| Algae bioreactors | 20 m² | **40 m²** |
| Aquaponics system | — | **30 m² fish tanks + grow beds** |
| LED supplemental lighting | — | **Full-spectrum, 18 h photoperiod** |
| Growing method | Soil-based | **Hybrid: hydroponics + soil beds** |

##### 4.2 Crop Selection and Yield Targets

Crop selection is optimised for caloric density, growth speed, nutritional completeness, and CO_{2}-to-O_{2} conversion efficiency:

| Crop | Area (m²) | Yield (kg/m²/yr) | Calories (kcal/kg) | Annual kcal | Role |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Potatoes** | 200 | 15 | 770 | 2,310,000 | Staple carbohydrate |
| **Soybeans** | 150 | 3 | 1,460 | 657,000 | Protein + oil |
| **Wheat** | 200 | 4 | 3,390 | 2,712,000 | Staple grain |
| **Rice** | 100 | 5 | 1,300 | 650,000 | Staple grain |
| **Lettuce/greens** | 150 | 20 | 150 | 450,000 | Vitamins + minerals |
| **Tomatoes** | 100 | 30 | 180 | 540,000 | Vitamins + morale |
| **Sweet potatoes** | 100 | 12 | 860 | 1,032,000 | Carbohydrate + vitamin A |
| **Spirulina (algae)** | 40 | 50 (dry) | 2,900 | 5,800,000 | Protein + O_{2} production |
| **Tilapia (aquaponics)** | 30 | 8 (fish/m²/yr × 0.5 kg) | 960 | 115,200 | Animal protein |
| **Total** | **1,070** | | | **~14,266,200** | |
| **Required** (4 crew × 2,500 kcal/day × 668 sols) | | | | **~6,680,000** | |

The system produces roughly **2× the minimum caloric requirement**, providing a safety buffer consistent with Biosphere 2's lesson that agricultural shortfalls are the most dangerous failure mode (crew lost 16% body weight despite "the highest producing farm in the world").

##### 4.3 Aquaponics Integration

A closed-loop fish–plant system provides protein diversification and nutrient cycling:

```
┌─────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐
│  Fish Tanks │────>│ Biofilter    │────>│ Grow Beds    │
│  (Tilapia)  │     │ (NH_{3}→NO_{3}⁻)   │     │ (Lettuce,    │
│  30 m²      │     │              │     │  tomatoes)   │
│  28°C       │     └──────────────┘     │              │
│             │<─────────────────────────│ Return water │
└─────────────┘                          └──────────────┘
      │                                         │
      ▼                                         ▼
  Fish waste                              Clean water
  (fertiliser)                            (back to tanks)
```

- **Fish species:** Tilapia (*Oreochromis niloticus*) — hardy, fast-growing, omnivorous, previously used in Biosphere 2's rice–azolla pond system
- **Feed:** Spirulina + crop residue + insect meal (black soldier fly larvae fed on food waste)
- **Yield:** ~120 kg fish/year (30 g protein/day for 4 crew)

##### 4.4 Lighting System

Mars receives only ~43% of Earth's solar irradiance (590 W/m² peak at Mars vs. 1,361 W/m²). During global dust storms (lasting 2–8 weeks), solar input can drop to 10–20% of nominal.

**Supplemental LED array:**
- Full-spectrum LEDs (red 660 nm + blue 450 nm + white) — optimised for photosynthetically active radiation (PAR)
- Power requirement: ~50 W/m² × 1,200 m² effective area × 18 h/day = **1,080 kWh/day** at full power
- During clear conditions: LEDs supplement natural sunlight (reduce to ~30% power)
- During dust storms: LEDs operate at 100% to maintain crop growth
- Light scheduling: 18 h light / 6 h dark cycle (optimised for most crop species)

