#### 8. In-Situ Resource Utilisation (ISRU)

##### 8.1 Available Martian Resources

| Resource | Source | Abundance | Processing |
|---|---|---|---|
| **SiO_{2} (silicon dioxide)** | Regolith (~45\% SiO_{2}) | Abundant | Glass, silicone rubber, aerogel |
| **Fe_{2}O_{3} (iron oxide)** | Regolith (~18\% Fe_{2}O_{3}) | Abundant | Iron/steel for tools, structures |
| **CO_{2}** | Atmosphere (95.3\%) | Effectively unlimited | Sabatier → CH_{4} + O_{2}; feedstock for plant growth |
| **N_{2}** | Atmosphere (2.7\%) | Limited but extractable | Fertiliser (Haber–Bosch requires H_{2} + N_{2}) |
| **H_{2}O (ice)** | Subsurface ice deposits | Variable by location | Water, H_{2} (electrolysis), O_{2} |
| **Ar (argon)** | Atmosphere (1.6\%) | Available | Inert gas for welding, fire suppression |
| **Al_{2}O_{3}, TiO_{2}, MgO** | Regolith | Minor components | Aluminium, titanium extraction (long-term) |

##### 8.2 ISRU Processing Chain

**Phase 1 (from Sol 1): Atmospheric Processing**
- CO_{2} collection + Sabatier reaction: CO_{2} + 4H_{2} → CH_{4} + 2H_{2}O
- Produces methane (fuel/heating) + water
- Water electrolysis: 2H_{2}O → 2H_{2} + O_{2}
- Oxygen for atmosphere; hydrogen recycled to Sabatier

**Phase 2 (from Sol 100): Regolith Processing**
- Regolith collection by robotic systems ([DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.15455156](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15455156))
- Silica extraction for glass repair and silicone rubber production
- Iron oxide reduction for basic metal tools
- Regolith sintering for construction bricks

**Phase 3 (from Sol 300): Chemical Manufacturing**
- Haber–Bosch process (N_{2} + H_{2} → NH_{3}) — requires significant energy but enables fertiliser independence
- Perchlorate reduction from regolith — detoxification of Martian soil for agriculture
- Water extraction from subsurface ice deposits

##### 8.3 ISRU Facility Requirements

| Equipment | Mass (kg) | Power (kW) | Location |
|---|---|---|---|
| CO_{2} collector + compressor | 200 | 2 | Exterior |
| Sabatier reactor | 150 | 1 | Temperate zone |
| Water electrolysis unit | 100 | 5 | Temperate zone |
| Regolith processing oven | 300 | 8 | Exterior (shielded) |
| Haber–Bosch mini-reactor | 200 | 3 | Temperate zone |
| **Total** | **950** | **19 peak** | |

