#### 10. Safety and Emergency Systems

##### 10.1 Emergency Scenarios and Responses

| Scenario | Detection | Response | Shelter Time |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Rapid depressurisation** | Pressure sensors (< 65 kPa alarm) | Seal affected zone; don emergency masks; locate and patch breach | Minutes |
| **Fire** | Smoke + thermal sensors | CO_{2} extinguishers; seal compartment; ventilate after extinguishing | Minutes–hours |
| **Solar particle event** | Space weather alert (8 min warning from Earth) | Crew to storm shelter; remain until all-clear | 24–72 hours |
| **Dust storm (major)** | Atmospheric opacity sensors | Load priority mode; LED agriculture; battery conservation | Weeks |
| **Medical emergency** | Crew report; vital monitors | Stabilise; telemedicine consultation; surgical intervention if trained | — |
| **Communication loss** | Signal timeout | Autonomous operations per standing protocols; antenna diagnostic | Days–weeks |
| **Water system failure** | Flow + quality sensors | Switch to emergency reservoir (10 m³ = 100 days at reduced use) | Days |
| **Crop failure** | Visual + sensor monitoring | Emergency rations (6 months stored); accelerated replanting | Weeks–months |

